WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
CMMC is not solely a compliance-team initiative.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.000
The people who design systems, administer accounts, develop applications,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.220
manage contracts, operate services, handle information,

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.765
and oversee suppliers all affect the security outcome.

00:00:13.765 --> 00:00:15.880
Leadership establishes accountability and resources.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.500
Executives and program owners decide priorities, approve risk decisions,

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.025
resolve ownership conflicts,

00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:25.280
and ensure that contract commitments are supported by realistic staffing, technology,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.100
and schedules.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.730
Contract and program teams identify clauses, information requirements,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.660
flow-down obligations, delivery expectations, and supplier relationships.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.685
They help technical teams understand what work and information are actually covered.

00:00:37.685 --> 00:00:41.160
Engineers and architects shape system boundaries, data flows, approved services,

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.515
segmentation, identity, encryption, logging, backups, and resilience.

00:00:45.515 --> 00:00:49.375
Design choices can reduce scope and make required safeguards easier to operate

00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:50.035
consistently.

00:00:50.035 --> 00:00:54.785
Administrators and IT teams manage accounts, endpoints, networks, configurations, updates,

00:00:54.785 --> 00:00:56.600
monitoring, support, and change.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.980
Daily operational discipline determines whether documented controls remain true after an

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:01.960
assessment.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.260
Developers and product teams contribute through secure development,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:08.510
controlled repositories, dependency management, testing, access restrictions,

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:13.500
change review, and proper handling of FCI or CUI in development and support workflows.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.470
Employees need to recognize protected information, use approved systems,

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.470
follow access and reporting procedures, complete training,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.500
and avoid moving contract data into unapproved email, storage, collaboration,

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.330
or artificial-intelligence services.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.806
Security and compliance teams coordinate policy, risk, evidence, monitoring, incidents,

00:01:29.806 --> 00:01:32.115
internal review, and assessment activity.

00:01:32.115 --> 00:01:35.610
Their role is strongest when integrated with operations rather than functioning as a

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:36.800
separate paperwork layer.
